{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>לֵאמֹר / saying.</b> One needs to know to whom he is to say it. If to Phinehas — there would have been no need to say afterward ״לָכֵן אֱמֹר״, since He had already said that he should say the matters to him. Moreover, the sequence of the verses will indicate that this is not so." "<b>And it appears</b> that by this He intended that he say to Israel the matters stated in the passage, with the intent that they recognize the good deed that Phinehas did for them and not hate him on account of his killing the prince, and for what resulted from his act — that the angel withdrew from them as much as he did — as they of blessed memory said (Sanhedrin 82b), as I shall explain nearby:"], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:14:09.854866024Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}